  "id": "hierarchical-design",
  "term": "hierarchical design",
  "definition": "Hierarchical design is an approach to building a system by arranging it into ordered layers, with each layer handling a different function and supporting the next. In the source, it means structuring a library information model into levels such as data input, processing, knowledge building, service use, and user interaction so complex information can be managed more coherently.",
